WwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-05-02T16:59:01Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T17:06:51Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.4 iOS\n\n### System information\n\niOS\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn Godot 4.4 on iOS my app will not pass app review if it would be publishing the documents directory to Files/Local Storage because the Godot shader cache is in it instead of being in the Application Support directory or cache directory where it belongs.\n\nI’d recommend placing the shader cache in the Application Support directory if the reasoning was avoiding system cache purges.\n\nI haven't checked, but if Godot does put the files in the Application Support directory conditionally in production then a readme.txt should be placed next to shader_cache with information for developers deploying in XCode and TestFlight environments.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIn the iOS export dialog add \n```xml\n<key>LSSupportsOpeningDocumentsInPlace</key>\n<true/>\n<key>UIFileSharingEnabled</key>\n<true/>\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nExport to iOS, install using Xcode","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106028/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106028/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}